  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Child Health through Strengthening the Management Capacity of Intestinal Parasitic Infections in Loreto, Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Located in Loreto Region of Peru, Iquitos is one of the poorest areas in Peru, with impoverished neighborhoods formed along the Itaya River, which connects to the Amazon River. According to statistics from the Health Department of Loreto Region, as of 2022, the prevalence of anemia among children under 12 in the Belen area is 57.2 percentages. Given the local conditions, inadequate nutrition intake and unsanitary environments are presumed to contribute to childhood anemia due to intestinal parasite infections. However, both the Peruvian central government and local governments show limited interest in prevention and management of intestinal parasite infections. Therefore, the need for support in this regard is evident. Improving parasitic control services for children.&#xB85C;&#xB808;&#xD1A0; &#xC9C0;&#xC5ED; &#xC544;&#xB3D9;(3~12&#xC138;) &#xB300;&#xC0C1; &#xC7A5;&#xB0B4;&#xAE30;&#xC0DD;&#xCDA9; &#xAD00;&#xB9AC; &#xAC1C;&#xC120;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide Parasitic Infection Testing and Basic Health Check-ups, Provide Deworming and Nutritional Supplements, and Medication Guidance, Improve School WASH Environment (Small-scale Facility Renovation), Awareness Raising Activities on Personal Hygiene Management, Awareness Raising Activities on Safe Water Usage, Awareness Raising Activities on Parasitic Infection, Provide Parenting Education for pre-school students parents, Train Healthcare Workers (Diagnosis), Provide Equipment for Parasitic Infection Diagnosis and Improve Health Facility Environment, Train School Teachers (Prevention and Control), Develop Intestinal Parasitic Infection Management Guidelines, Establishing Parasitic Infection Network and Support Regular Meetings, Organizing Symposiums and Workshops to Share Information and Experience,</narrative>
  </description>
